\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{Gasket graphs}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{The \newvocab{gasket graph} #{G_n} and its cells are defined
as follows. #{V_0} has three vertices, and #{G_0} has one edge
joining each pair. That triangle is the unique #{0}-cell.}

\p{Suppose the cells of #{G_n} are defined. Each edge of
#{G_n} receives one new midpoint, and #{V_{n+1}} consists of
#{V_n} together with those midpoints. In an #{n}-cell with
corners #{A,B,C}, write #{a} for the midpoint of #{BC},
#{b} for the midpoint of #{AC}, and #{c} for the midpoint of
#{AB}. The three #{(n+1)}-cells inside this cell are the
triangles on the vertices #{\{A,b,c\}}, #{\{B,a,c\}}, and
#{\{C,a,b\}}, with all three edges of each triangle present.
The edge set of #{G_{n+1}} is the set of all edges of these
#{(n+1)}-cells, as the parent cell runs through the cells of
#{G_n}.}
